course: dictionary
lesson: 10936
title: Vulnerable: easily hurt or at risk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vulnerable means easily hurt, harmed or attacked, in body or feelings. Look at the words around it for clues. «Giant pandas were moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016 after their numbers rose.» Endangered means in great danger of dying out, so vulnerable must be a less serious level of risk: still at risk, but less so.
explain: Vulnerable can also mean open to something bad. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «The Arabian oryx was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972» shows the danger, and the later change to vulnerable shows that the animals were no longer in such great danger. Ask: what would fit here?
explain: People can be vulnerable too. Vulnerable people need extra protection, such as young children, very old people or people who are ill. When you feel vulnerable, you feel unsafe or open to being hurt, and that is why adults help to protect those who are vulnerable.
fact: Vulnerable is an adjective, so it describes a person, an animal or a thing.
fact: «Vulnerable» means easily hurt, harmed or attacked, in body or feelings.
fact: Vulnerable people need extra protection, such as young children, very old people or people who are ill.
fact: Useful phrases: «vulnerable to», «vulnerable children», «feel vulnerable», «a vulnerable species».
fact: «Giant pandas» moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016, because their numbers grew to about 1,800 in the wild.
exercise: «Giant pandas were moved from endangered to vulnerable in 2016.» What does this change show? | *It means they are still at risk, but in less danger than before | It means they have all died out | It means they now live only in zoos | It means they are now completely safe
exercise: «Vulnerable children need adults to keep them safe.» What does vulnerable mean here? | Loud and full of energy | Happy with lots of friends | Very clever and quick at school | *Easily hurt or harmed, so they need protection
exercise: «She feels vulnerable when she walks home alone in the dark.» Which feeling does vulnerable describe? | Proud and brave | Bored and sleepy | *Open to being hurt and unsafe | Hungry and tired
test: «He is vulnerable to colds, so he wears a warm coat in winter.» What does vulnerable to colds mean? | Immune and never ill | *Easily caught by colds | Bright and cheerful all the time | Lost in the snow
test: Ellie is told: «Never share your password or address online, because people can use private details to make you vulnerable.» What does vulnerable mean here? | Happy and calm | Too tired to move | Very popular with other people | *Easily harmed, for example by someone who learns your private details
exam: Which sentence uses vulnerable correctly? | *Young children are vulnerable and need adults to protect them | Vulnerable is a type of bird that lives by the sea | The vulnerable cake was delicious and warm | The vulnerable sun shone brightly on the hills
